from the outside people's minds seem  like pretty straightforward places what  we hear people saying suggests a certain  logic order and coherence but inside the  mind it's a very different effort here  things are infinitely more complex  fractured and multi-layered and  confusing amidst the shadowy tangled  darkness one can imagine a single  brightly lit zone like a spotlight in a  cave the area that normally goes by the  term consciousness this is where we do  our rational thinking where ideas are  clarified where plans are put on a  systemic footing where we order and  clean up our thoughts but the key thing  about the way we work is that unless we  take very special measures most of what  is inside the mind will remain far  outside the spotlight of consciousness  in what we can call the unconscious  zones these unconscious zones contain  recesses and grottoes filled with  unknown disavowed thoughts and feeling  feelings is had without properly  experiencing emotions we felt without  properly registering here we find a  record of pretty much everything we've  ever seen where we've been to who we've  met and how we felt most of the time the  images are dormant and submerged then  occasionally but what can feel like  quite random points an image will  suddenly come back to us clear as day  suddenly we'll see Uncle Ernie or the  pier in Brighton or the train taking us  up the Matterhorn when we were nine a  lot of what lies in the unconscious are  warring things with frightened might  happen which we push out of  consciousness  we keep them at bay but the effort  creates a hum and Static of background  anxiety in the unconscious a desires  that can't find a place in our more  ordered sensible day-to-day lives there  are ideas we haven't some time to sort  out  and angry hurt feelings we haven't  digested the sadness we haven't dared to  feel when we speak of getting to know  ourselves but increasing self-knowledge  really what we mean is the task of  getting more active with the spotlight  of consciousness moving it around more  regularly in our minds more  systematically shining its beams into  unfamiliar corners so that we're less  surprised than frightened by some of  what we have in our mind our founding  belief is that the more of the mind we  can light up with consciousness the more  peaceful coherent and focus we can be  this is what it means to lead an  examined life to try to become less of a  stranger to oneself by illuminating our  minds with a spotlight of consciousness  you
 

